  m_Name: Recipe_DillPickleChips
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GrandmasHouse.Data.RecipeData
  displayName: Dill Pickle Chips
  fill: 0
  label: {fileID: 2100000, guid: 6f707c382f6b06c4d8b640717e65cf19, type: 2}
  slicesPerJar: 20
  needsDill: 1
  garlicPerJar: 2
  peppercornPinches: 0
  brineLine: 0.88
  brineEnough: 0.75
  vinegarShare: 0.5
  saltScoops: 2
  heatSeconds: 8
  potPerJar: 0.2
  processMinutes: 10
  cardText: '(stand-in until Grandma''s own card is added)


    Makes about 6 pints.

    4
    lbs small pickling cucumbers, sliced 1/4 inch

    6 heads fresh dill

    6
    cloves garlic


    Brine: 3 cups white vinegar, 3 cups water, 1/4 cup pickling
    salt. Bring to a boil.


    Put a head of dill and a clove of garlic in each
    hot jar. Pack the cucumbers in snug. Pour the hot brine over, leaving 1/2 inch
    at the top. Wipe the rims, put on lids and rings, and process pints 10 minutes
    in a boiling water bath.'
